{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-51346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $h(x)=5-10x,$ find ${({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${h}^{-1}(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-51346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=5-10x,$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=5-10y\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={h}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(5-10y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =-10 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${h}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={h}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{h}^{-1}(x)] & =-\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ {({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-51346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2e156de1335d27406e8b355259b19f7acc6c7f4ff91a253871efe5a495eeb82e"} {"question" "q-51346" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-51346" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{10}"] ["math" "10{h}^{-1}(x)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{10{h}^{-1}(x)}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{5-10{h}^{-1}(x)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-51346" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{10}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-32630" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $h(x)=2{x}^{5}+3{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}+6,$ find ${({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${h}^{-1}(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-32630" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=2{x}^{5}+3{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}+6,$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=2{y}^{5}+3{y}^{4}-{y}^{3}+6\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={h}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{5}+3{y}^{4}-{y}^{3}+6) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =10{y}^{4}+12{y}^{3}-3{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{10{y}^{4}+12{y}^{3}-3{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${h}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={h}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{h}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{1}{10({h}^{-1}(x))^{4}+12({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}-3({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}} \\\\ {({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{10({h}^{-1}(x))^{4}+12({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}-3({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-32630" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2e156de1335d27406e8b355259b19f7acc6c7f4ff91a253871efe5a495eeb82e"} {"question" "q-32630" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-32630" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{10({h}^{-1}(x))^{4}+6({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}-({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}}"] ["math" "10({h}^{-1}(x))^{4}+12({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}-3({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}"] ["math" "5({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+12({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}-{h}^{-1}(x)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{10({h}^{-1}(x))^{4}+12({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}-3({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5({h}^{-1}(x))^{5}+5({h}^{-1}(x))^{4}-3({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-32630" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{10({h}^{-1}(x))^{4}+12({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}-3({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-47990" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $g(x)=-{x}^{2}+\\frac{2}{x},$ find ${({g}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${g}^{-1}(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-47990" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=-{x}^{2}+\\frac{2}{x},$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=-{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{y}\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={g}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{y}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =-2y-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =-\\frac{2{y}^{3}+2}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2{y}^{3}+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${g}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={g}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{g}^{-1}(x)] & =-\\frac{({g}^{-1}(x))^{2}}{2({g}^{-1}(x))^{3}+2} \\\\ {({g}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{({g}^{-1}(x))^{2}}{2({g}^{-1}(x))^{3}+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-47990" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2e156de1335d27406e8b355259b19f7acc6c7f4ff91a253871efe5a495eeb82e"} {"question" "q-47990" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-47990" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2{({g}^{-1}(x))}^{2}}{{({g}^{-1}(x))}^{3}+1}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2{g}^{-1}(x)}{{({g}^{-1}(x))}^{2}+2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{{({g}^{-1}(x))}^{2}}{2{({g}^{-1}(x))}^{3}+2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{{g}^{-1}(x)}{2{g}^{-1}(x)+2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{{g}^{-1}(x)}{{({g}^{-1}(x))}^{3}+2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-47990" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{{({g}^{-1}(x))}^{2}}{2{({g}^{-1}(x))}^{3}+2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-3301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x)=12x+5,$ find ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${f}^{-1}(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-3301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=12x+5,$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=12y+5\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={f}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(12y+5) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${f}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={f}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{f}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{1}{12} \\\\ {({f}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-3301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2e156de1335d27406e8b355259b19f7acc6c7f4ff91a253871efe5a495eeb82e"} {"question" "q-3301" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-3301" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12{f}^{-1}(x)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{12{f}^{-1}(x)}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{12{f}^{-1}(x)+5}"] ["math" "{f}^{-1}(x)+12"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-3301" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{12}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-3298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${({g}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$  as a function of ${g}^{-1}(x),$ if $g(x)=8{x}^{2}+x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-3298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=8{x}^{2}+x,$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=8{y}^{2}+y\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={g}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(8{y}^{2}+y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =16y+1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{16y+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${g}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={g}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{g}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{1}{16{g}^{-1}(x)+1} \\\\ {({g}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{16{g}^{-1}(x)+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-3298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2e156de1335d27406e8b355259b19f7acc6c7f4ff91a253871efe5a495eeb82e"} {"question" "q-3298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-3298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{({g}^{-1}(x))^{2}+{g}^{-1}(x)}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{16({g}^{-1}(x))^{2}+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{16{g}^{-1}(x)+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{16{g}^{-1}(x)}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8({g}^{-1}(x))^{2}+{g}^{-1}(x)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-3298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{16{g}^{-1}(x)+1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-32646" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $h(x)={2}^{x+1},$ find ${({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${h}^{-1}(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-32646" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y={2}^{x+1},$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx={2}^{y+1}\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={h}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({2}^{y+1}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & ={2}^{y+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{2}^{y+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{2}^{-y}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${h}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={h}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{h}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{{2}^{-{h}^{-1}(x)}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{2}^{-{h}^{-1}(x)}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-32646" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2e156de1335d27406e8b355259b19f7acc6c7f4ff91a253871efe5a495eeb82e"} {"question" "q-32646" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-32646" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot {2}^{{h}^{-1}(x)}"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\cdot {2}^{-{h}^{-1}(x)}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{2}^{-{h}^{-1}(x)}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{2}^{-{h}^{-1}(x)}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{2}^{{h}^{-1}(x)}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-32646" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{2}^{-{h}^{-1}(x)}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-51347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $h(x)=\\sqrt{2x+5},$ find ${({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${h}^{-1}(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-51347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=\\sqrt{2x+5},$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{2y+5}\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={h}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\sqrt{2y+5}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}((2y+5)^{1/2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{1}{2}(2y+5)^{-1/2}\\cdot 2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2y+5}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sqrt{2y+5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${h}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={h}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{h}^{-1}(x)] & =\\sqrt{2{h}^{-1}(x)+5} \\\\ {({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\sqrt{2{h}^{-1}(x)+5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8093fdc371c1a377598fe9ac8d"} {"question" "q-51347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2e156de1335d27406e8b355259b19f7acc6c7f4ff91a253871efe5a495eeb82e"} {"question" "q-51347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979277/state.json" "file_sha256" "92636fd31d02c0dd27ff45c17964c0bb650eeb8